by nicolas-grekas at 2026-09-08T19:22:44Z

@dgafka you are 100% right, I used your article as a starting point and worked with an LLM to send those PRs. So yes, big thanks for that article.

What I got wrong is the credit. The descriptions reuse your examples, the order subscribers, the loan flow, the payment webhook, and none of them says where the analysis comes from. I'm adding a note to each PR: they started from your article, and they are proposals open for discussion, nothing more yet.

As you might see in most of them, there were preexisting issues in the Symfony repo describing those as desired capabilities, yet nobody had achieved them in Symfony itself, a community-bandwidth issue of the pre-LLM world. It's now within reach, and your article is what turned a list of old issues into a coherent picture.

They are not ports of Ecotone though. Several go a different way on purpose, Messenger keeps routing by class and has no channel concept.

Ecotone running inside Symfony is a good thing, and your article is the best explanation of what the fuller version of this looks like.

